# 6. The failure to re-enter is the strongest problem

Pratt told Bennett that she would recommend re-entering equities “when conditions stabilized.” That statement matters.

Once Pratt recommended a tactical exit strategy, the reasonableness of the strategy depended heavily on having a re-entry discipline. A tactical de-risking recommendation is incomplete if the advisor does not have a rational process for deciding when to get back in.

