The strongest issue is the repeated switching among substantially similar large-cap equity mutual funds while imposing new front-end loads each time.

A mutual-fund switch may be appropriate if there is a genuine investment rationale, such as:

- A meaningful change in investment objective;
- A material difference in risk exposure;
- A substantially better cost structure;
- Manager or strategy concerns;
- Tax considerations;
- Portfolio rebalancing needs; or
