Thomas asked none of these questions and did not update the account profile. That is a serious problem under both Reg BI’s Care Obligation and FINRA Rule 2090.

The later divorce settlement requiring Brian to pay $170,000 confirms the materiality of the information Thomas failed to investigate. The violation does not depend solely on hindsight, but the outcome illustrates why the omitted inquiry mattered.

